      "id": "IC_kwDOBjach872mLCa",
      "author": {
        "login": "MeeSiing"
      },
      "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Hi @corismall, I have gathered more info and considering to create preneoplastic lesion as a new term. \nI need to know if this updated definition represents the concept you want.\nPreneoplastic lesion def = A precancerous condition characterized by accumulation of some molecular alterations necessary for malignant transformation in a clonal proliferation of cells, representing an intermediate stage in carcinogenesis with increased risk of progression to invasive neoplasia. \nDo you think preneoplastic lesion is a subtype of pre-maglinat neoplasm (def =A disease of cellular proliferation that results in abnormal growths in the body, which do not invade or destroy the surrounding tissue but, given enough time, will transform into a cancer)?\nIf yes, I can create preneoplastic lesion as a child term under pre-maglinat neoplasm.  ",
